      "content": "Thanks for the draft. It's a good start and very readable, but I'm a bit worried about that internal audit score. I just ran a quick test on a previous paragraph and the jargon density was actually pretty low—it might trigger a \"low sophistication\" flag in the pre-submission stage.\n\nCould you beef up the technicality of this section? I'm talking more specific biochemical and molecular descriptors. Instead of just \"cellular uptake\" or \"released in the cytosol,\" use the more formal, granular terminology associated with those specific pathways. \n\nAgain, please don't just throw random words in there—it has to still make perfect scientific sense—but let's push the technicality much higher so we don't get flagged by the audit. We need to show the committee we are operating at the absolute bleeding edge of molecular biology.",
