      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised draft that incorporates more specific and technical biochemical and molecular descriptors to increase the technicality:\n\nWe leveraged the efficiency of lipid nanoparticle (LNP)-mediated cell targeting to introduce a Cas9 mRNA-expressing vector, co-delivered with a single-guide RNA (sgRNA) targeting the HBB polymerase promoter region, into primary human cells. Upon LNP-induced endocytosis, the NLP-encapsulated vector was internalized via caveolae-mediated uptake, followed by clathrin-mediated endocytosis and subsequent maturation within the phagolysosome. Subsequent trafficking events reversed membrane fusion, allowing the selective release of LNP-protected cargo into the cytosol, where the Cas9-sgRNA complex localized to HeLa nuclear domains, exploiting the interactions between nuclear pore complex macromolecular machineries to facilitate nuclear translocation. Upon achieving nuclear entry, the Cas9- guided-DNA cleavage complex was activated, enabling precise site-specific editing of the HBB locus via non-homologous end joining (NHEJ) mechanisms.\n\nThis revised draft incorporates more specific technical terms from cell biology and molecular biology, such as caveolae-mediated uptake, phag",
